{%- comment -%}
  A product's analytics fields as data attributes, read by
  frontend/scripts/analytics.js to build GA4 `items`. Output inside an opening
  tag. The element still needs `data-item` to count as a selectable item (a
  card or suggestion link); the PDP carries these fields without it, so a click
  anywhere on the page is not taken for a product selection.

  `item_id` copies the format the Google & YouTube app sends with its own
  ecommerce events (shopify_ZZ_<product>_<variant>). GA4 only credits a
  purchase to the list an item was selected from when the two ids match.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Shopify product object (required)
  - variant: {Object} Variant to describe. Default: the selected or first
                      available one, which is what a card shows and quick-adds.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign item_variant = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign item_price = item_variant.price | default: product.price | divided_by: 100.0
-%}
data-item-id="shopify_ZZ_{{ product.id }}_{{ item_variant.id }}"
data-item-name="{{ product.title | escape }}"
data-item-brand="{{ product.vendor | escape }}"
data-item-category="{{ product.type | escape }}"
data-item-price="{{ item_price }}"
data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
